30 Oct: closing. The evaluation was done last week on F02 + F03; the ICM-45686 is the production DVNC vibration reference (John, 21 Oct).
John added the timing this week:
- vibration leads sound by at most ~1.4 ms on the one sensor pair with no clock uncertainty (both through one ADAU1372);
- DEV-A and DEV-B capture clocks differ by 51.6 ppm (~90 ms per 30 min), so the next rig runs every codec on one clock;
- DEV-B's ADXL354 has a constant 148 µs delay and can stand in as the timing reference the ICM-45686 lacks.
Evidence: chris/golf/2026-W44_fleet_week.md; reports/john/2026-10-26_imu_audio_timebase.html (team repo).
